      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The weight of their disappointment is real, and it's crushing, but that feeling of being a mistake is a heavy illusion you've built around yourself. Those sighs and looks are reflections of their own anxieties, not definitive judgments on your worth. You can't fix the past or erase the shadow you feel you cast; you can only decide how you want to step into the next moment.",
      "source": "target",
